     <rdf:li>Sea Fighter</rdf:li>
     <rdf:li>USMC</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Bag>
   </dc:subject>
   <dc:description>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">160729-N-PO203-999 GULF OF MEXICO (Jul. 29, 2016) This composite photograph shows the launch sequence of a Coyote air vehicle as part of the Office of Naval Research (ONR)-Low-Cost Unmanned Aerial Vehicle Swarming Technology (LOCUST) at-sea experiment conducted aboard Sea Fighter (FSF 1) off the coast of Florida. The experiment is designed to develop and demonstrate the set-up, launch, formation, control and tasking of 30 small air vehicles in a coordinated autonomous swarming behavior. (U.S. Navy photo by John F. Williams/Released)</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
   </dc:description>
   <dc:creator>
    <rdf:Seq>
     <rdf:li>John F. Williams</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Seq>
   </dc:creator>
   <dc:title>
    <rdf:Alt>
     <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">160729-N-PO203-999</rdf:li>
    </rdf:Alt>
